<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="d00ab9b0-114c-557a-baf2-ab2501b8ae5b" activityNameId="bd6f17e9-1007-58ef-8bda-60dc3857641e" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Operation, average train</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Operation, average train
Data for the operation of average trains in Belgium (regional trains, S-Bahn, long distance-trains), the data has been determined top down by International Rail Statistics. Particulate emissions due to abrasion of rail tracks, wheels, brakes and overhead contact line is included according to Swiss situation. Emission of sulphur hexafluoride (SF6) occurring during conversion at traction substations are accounted for.;
UUID: a0a0cfae-58d2-3198-8890-fbc6e22a985d
The inventory includes the actual energy consumption  (11000 t Diesel and 1121 GWh of electricity) due to traction of passenger trains.
Location: Data refers to average transport conditions
Technology: all technologies included, the train is operated with the country electricity mix.
Time period: all data is based on situation in the year 2000, except the specific energy consumption per pkm (year 2007)
Production volume: 9932 Mio. pkm in 2007
Sampling: UIC-studies and own assumptions 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_a0a0cfae-58d2-3198-8890-fbc6e22a985d.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="f5f722ed-cace-5738-bbab-d3554c24a58a" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
